1
00:01:28,866 --> 00:01:34,705
GOOD GRIEF, GIRLS' DAY

2
00:01:34,905 --> 00:01:36,073
"KAMEARI SHOPPING DISTRICT"

3
00:01:38,242 --> 00:01:43,214
I want some more midnight snacks

4
00:01:43,414 --> 00:01:45,482
And some juice—

5
00:01:45,683 --> 00:01:46,584
Huh?

6
00:01:46,917 --> 00:01:48,919
"GIRLS' DAY SALE"

7
00:01:50,421 --> 00:01:51,689
Blegh!

8
00:01:56,493 --> 00:02:03,567
Spend over 1,000 yen at our shopping district and get a free photo sticker.

9
00:02:06,303 --> 00:02:07,838
Say cheese!

10
00:02:11,208 --> 00:02:11,976
Ryo-san!

11
00:02:12,209 --> 00:02:15,579
There's a Girls' Day knockout tournament over there. Wanna play?

12
00:02:15,779 --> 00:02:18,916
I hate March 3! Get out of the way!

13
00:02:21,752 --> 00:02:23,888
-What's wrong with Ryo-san? -Dunno.

14
00:02:24,088 --> 00:02:27,424
Let's light the candles in the lanterns

15
00:02:27,625 --> 00:02:29,860
Oh right, today is Girls' Day, isn't it?

16
00:02:30,527 --> 00:02:32,630
Yes. Look, isn't she cute?

17
00:02:32,863 --> 00:02:37,768
-They never get too old for Girls' Day. -Right.

18
00:02:38,402 --> 00:02:39,169
Good morning.

19
00:02:41,338 --> 00:02:42,873
-Good morning. -Good morning.

20
00:02:43,140 --> 00:02:45,276
Hmm? Where's Ryotsu?

21
00:02:45,476 --> 00:02:47,177
He went out on patrol.

22
00:02:47,544 --> 00:02:51,181
Patrol? More like slacking off somewhere.

23
00:02:51,782 --> 00:02:53,918
Ryo-chan can't resist a festival.

24
00:02:54,251 --> 00:02:56,787
Yes, but today is Girls' Day.

25
00:02:56,987 --> 00:03:00,424
Nothing to do with a caveman like Ryotsu.

26
00:03:03,627 --> 00:03:04,828
Who'd drop their ID?

27
00:03:06,263 --> 00:03:07,765
It's Ryotsu's, of course.

28
00:03:11,368 --> 00:03:13,003
This is hilarious...

29
00:03:13,203 --> 00:03:14,505
What is it, Chief?

30
00:03:15,105 --> 00:03:18,208
Get a load of what I just discovered. Look, here.

31
00:03:18,442 --> 00:03:19,376
"DOB: MARCH 3"

32
00:03:19,910 --> 00:03:22,179
-March... -Third?!

33
00:03:22,580 --> 00:03:23,514
Ryo-chan's...

34
00:03:24,014 --> 00:03:26,183
His birthday. It's today!

35
00:03:26,383 --> 00:03:28,185
Which means...

36
00:03:28,686 --> 00:03:31,956
Ryo-san was born on Girls' Day?

37
00:03:34,792 --> 00:03:37,461
Oh dear! Ryo-chan, of all people!

38
00:03:37,661 --> 00:03:39,830
It doesn't fit his image at all.

39
00:03:40,030 --> 00:03:42,800
Who couldn't laugh at that?

40
00:03:43,934 --> 00:03:44,702
Hmm?

41
00:03:45,235 --> 00:03:47,204
-Hey, Ryo-san. -Yo!

42
00:03:47,538 --> 00:03:49,873
Ugh, damn it.

43
00:03:50,975 --> 00:03:53,377
Oh! Good morning, Chief!

44
00:03:54,211 --> 00:03:58,716
I was just out on patrol, keeping the neighborhood safe.

45
00:03:58,949 --> 00:04:00,084
I see.

46
00:04:00,317 --> 00:04:02,553
You took your police ID, right?

47
00:04:03,187 --> 00:04:06,090
Of course. I keep it safely in my pocket.

48
00:04:06,323 --> 00:04:07,558
Huh? That's odd.

49
00:04:07,791 --> 00:04:09,526
Did I put it here? Um...

50
00:04:09,727 --> 00:04:11,996
Here, you dropped it.

51
00:04:13,731 --> 00:04:15,799
Oh, thank you.

52
00:04:15,999 --> 00:04:17,434
Be careful next time.

53
00:04:18,535 --> 00:04:21,905
Oh, by the way, isn't it someone's birthday today?

54
00:04:22,206 --> 00:04:23,674
-Gulp! -Um...

55
00:04:23,874 --> 00:04:26,010
Who was it now? Terai?

56
00:04:26,210 --> 00:04:27,678
My birthday is May 5.

57
00:04:27,878 --> 00:04:29,346
That's Boys' Day.

58
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:34,051
Oh, a fine birthday fit for a man. Right, Ryotsu?

59
00:04:34,351 --> 00:04:35,753
Well, yeah...

60
00:04:35,986 --> 00:04:37,454
Reiko-san, yours is...

61
00:04:37,688 --> 00:04:38,756
July 7.

62
00:04:38,989 --> 00:04:40,391
Oh, the Star Festival.

63
00:04:40,591 --> 00:04:44,528
A romantic and feminine day. Isn't that right, Ryotsu?

64
00:04:44,728 --> 00:04:45,529
Yeah, yeah.

65
00:04:46,063 --> 00:04:50,367
But there's an even more romantic and feminine day. For example...

66
00:04:50,567 --> 00:04:53,871
-March... -The third.

67
00:04:54,772 --> 00:04:56,540
You mean Girls' Day, right?

68
00:04:56,740 --> 00:05:00,944
Yes! My birthday is March 3!

69
00:05:01,545 --> 00:05:04,281
Oh, really? I never knew.

70
00:05:04,481 --> 00:05:05,616
Yes you did.

71
00:05:05,849 --> 00:05:08,052
It's fine. Don't worry about it.

72
00:05:08,252 --> 00:05:11,789
Lots of men are born on March 3.

73
00:05:12,022 --> 00:05:14,858
Girls' Day just doesn't fit your image, that's all.

74
00:05:15,059 --> 00:05:17,127
Doesn't bother me one bit.

75
00:05:19,430 --> 00:05:23,701
What bothers me is ever since I was a kid, nothing good ever came on my birthday.

76
00:05:23,901 --> 00:05:24,702
Huh?

77
00:05:25,135 --> 00:05:29,907
It first started when I was in elementary school.

78
00:05:30,174 --> 00:05:32,943
I was making a set of cardboard dolls for a local girl,

79
00:05:33,143 --> 00:05:35,946
and I was lining them up on some stairs.

80
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:40,317
I slipped and fell down the stairs in a really bad way.

81
00:05:40,517 --> 00:05:41,251
Oh dear.

82
00:05:41,719 --> 00:05:44,788
Then in middle school, I drank some sake and got drunk,

83
00:05:44,988 --> 00:05:48,492
and I fell into the Sumida River and got swept out to sea.

84
00:05:48,725 --> 00:05:53,163
In high school, a girl caught me looking at porn and hung me out to dry.

85
00:05:53,363 --> 00:05:58,168
Everyone threw me under the bus, and I got left out of Girls' Day.

86
00:05:58,635 --> 00:06:01,338
Whenever I gamble on this day, I always lose big.

87
00:06:01,538 --> 00:06:04,007
I once lost my pay while fleeing creditors.

88
00:06:04,208 --> 00:06:07,611
Then I got attacked by crows and fell from high up.

89
00:06:08,378 --> 00:06:12,149
A dine and dash got a dog sicced on me. I got scammed by a peddler...

90
00:06:12,349 --> 00:06:15,452
My birthday is cursed!

91
00:06:15,652 --> 00:06:17,688
Any sympathy I had wore off fast.

92
00:06:17,921 --> 00:06:20,290
Sounds like you bring it all on yourself.

93
00:06:20,491 --> 00:06:24,928
Hmph. Say what you want, but I hate March 3!

94
00:06:25,496 --> 00:06:27,030
There's no need to overreact.

95
00:06:27,231 --> 00:06:29,166
You've just been unlucky so far.

96
00:06:29,533 --> 00:06:30,334
Oh, I know!

97
00:06:30,534 --> 00:06:33,003
Us girls are having a party at the dorm today.

98
00:06:33,203 --> 00:06:35,239
I'll give you a special invite.

99
00:06:35,472 --> 00:06:36,507
What, a party?

100
00:06:36,707 --> 00:06:38,008
Sure! I'll go!

101
00:06:38,542 --> 00:06:41,178
I was actually told just to invite Kei-chan.

102
00:06:41,378 --> 00:06:43,213
But I feel bad for Ryo-chan.

103
00:06:45,015 --> 00:06:46,817
So, will there be food?

104
00:06:47,017 --> 00:06:50,120
Of course. We'll have your favorite sushi there too.

105
00:06:50,354 --> 00:06:51,188
Hooray!

106
00:06:51,388 --> 00:06:53,791
I haven't had sushi for ages.

107
00:06:54,525 --> 00:06:56,960
Yes. This is Kameari Park Police Station.

108
00:06:57,161 --> 00:06:58,328
Huh? Yes, at once.

109
00:06:58,529 --> 00:07:02,199
Chief! Something's happened at Kingaichi-san's place!

110
00:07:02,399 --> 00:07:04,401
What? At that rich guy's house?

111
00:07:04,601 --> 00:07:06,036
Right. Let's go, Ryotsu.

112
00:07:06,236 --> 00:07:07,671
What? Me?

113
00:07:07,871 --> 00:07:09,239
Yes. Stop dawdling.

114
00:07:09,439 --> 00:07:11,041
No! Let go of me, Chief!

115
00:07:11,241 --> 00:07:13,177
I'm invited to the girls' dorm!

116
00:07:13,744 --> 00:07:16,580
-The sushi! The feast! -Poor thing.

117
00:07:16,813 --> 00:07:19,583
-Ryo-chan really does have bad luck. -Yeah.

118
00:07:20,450 --> 00:07:23,420
Listen up. The safety of the citizens comes first.

119
00:07:23,620 --> 00:07:27,925
It is the duty of the police to try to prevent any crime before it happens.

120
00:07:28,258 --> 00:07:29,893
Do you understand, Ryotsu?

121
00:07:30,227 --> 00:07:31,395
Get a move on!

122
00:07:31,595 --> 00:07:33,931
Kingaichi-san's house is over here.

123
00:07:34,298 --> 00:07:38,368
And I was looking forward to eating sushi. I really am unlucky.

124
00:07:38,569 --> 00:07:39,736
I bought some juice.

125
00:07:39,937 --> 00:07:42,706
-Thank you! Did you get Chunky Grape? -Yeah, I did.

126
00:07:43,774 --> 00:07:45,742
Hey, it backs onto the girls' dorm!

127
00:07:45,943 --> 00:07:48,445
It seems like my luck hasn't run out yet.

128
00:07:48,645 --> 00:07:50,614
Ryotsu! Hurry up!

129
00:07:50,848 --> 00:07:52,282
Coming!

130
00:07:59,957 --> 00:08:01,425
A threat?

131
00:08:01,625 --> 00:08:05,429
"I will take your hina dolls. Better watch out.

132
00:08:05,629 --> 00:08:08,198
From the Girls' Day Monster."

133
00:08:09,032 --> 00:08:11,134
This is the letter?

134
00:08:11,635 --> 00:08:12,736
That's right!

135
00:08:12,936 --> 00:08:15,439
What else would it be? A car sales flyer?

136
00:08:15,639 --> 00:08:18,909
It's clearly a bona fide threat letter!

137
00:08:19,109 --> 00:08:24,648
A law-abiding citizen is in trouble. Is the law not going to step up?

138
00:08:24,882 --> 00:08:26,250
N-No, I didn't mean...

139
00:08:26,450 --> 00:08:29,219
I've been beside myself since the letter came.

140
00:08:29,419 --> 00:08:31,521
I toss and turn all night.

141
00:08:31,755 --> 00:08:33,423
Of course we will help.

142
00:08:33,624 --> 00:08:37,494
It's the duty of the police to try to prevent any crime before it happens.

143
00:08:38,095 --> 00:08:41,999
But stealing hina dolls? Seems a bit silly for a "monster."

144
00:08:42,432 --> 00:08:45,269
-Could it be a little childish prank? -Ryotsu!

145
00:08:45,669 --> 00:08:50,607
Perhaps. But our hina dolls aren't just any old dolls.

146
00:08:50,807 --> 00:08:51,608
Huh?

147
00:08:51,808 --> 00:08:53,777
They're worth 500 million yen!

148
00:08:53,977 --> 00:08:56,913
500 million yen?

149
00:09:02,552 --> 00:09:06,823
That painting is worth 200 million yen. This sculpture cost about 300 million.

150
00:09:07,024 --> 00:09:08,692
A right bargain it was.

151
00:09:08,926 --> 00:09:11,361
200 or 300 million yen for these things?

152
00:09:12,329 --> 00:09:14,331
Hey! No touching!

153
00:09:14,531 --> 00:09:16,366
-Look with your eyes. -Hmph!

154
00:09:16,700 --> 00:09:18,869
And what about the hina dolls?

155
00:09:19,569 --> 00:09:23,540
I ordered them three years ago for my daughter, and they've finally arrived.

156
00:09:23,740 --> 00:09:25,876
Yes, this is my son, Tamaru.

157
00:09:26,109 --> 00:09:28,178
And this is my daughter, Amari.

158
00:09:28,979 --> 00:09:32,749
The names mean "Gain" and "Surplus." Quite the expectation on the kids.

159
00:09:33,050 --> 00:09:34,351
They're in here.

160
00:09:34,551 --> 00:09:35,352
In you go.

161
00:09:42,159 --> 00:09:47,030
It's a seven-tiered Heian Komachi hina doll set made by the illustrious Tamagoro!

162
00:09:47,230 --> 00:09:48,532
Wow, they're dazzling.

163
00:09:48,832 --> 00:09:54,204
A bespoke set by Living National Treasure Tamagoro brings beauty and custom to life.

164
00:09:54,404 --> 00:09:57,908
From the silk costumes to the Wajima lacquerware,

165
00:09:58,208 --> 00:10:00,310
everything has been expertly crafted.

166
00:10:00,510 --> 00:10:02,779
Even the best in their fields would marvel.

167
00:10:03,013 --> 00:10:06,249
The screens feature pure gold leaf, and the eyes are rubies.

168
00:10:06,683 --> 00:10:09,019
A Honneri head, diamonds on the fingers,

169
00:10:09,219 --> 00:10:13,590
and the base is adorned with countless sapphires and emeralds...

170
00:10:18,996 --> 00:10:21,231
That cost 500 million yen!

171
00:10:22,332 --> 00:10:23,100
You moron!

172
00:10:23,333 --> 00:10:27,471
Your salary could never pay for even one broken fan!

173
00:10:27,704 --> 00:10:28,905
All right, sorry!

174
00:10:29,539 --> 00:10:33,410
No need to worry. We'll keep a close eye on them.

175
00:10:33,610 --> 00:10:35,712
You'd better. I'm counting on you.

176
00:10:36,179 --> 00:10:38,181
Well, now I am parched.

177
00:10:38,815 --> 00:10:40,584
Hey! Bring some tea!

178
00:10:40,784 --> 00:10:42,586
The usual gold-leaf-infused kind!

179
00:10:42,786 --> 00:10:44,287
-Gold-leaf... -Infused tea?

180
00:10:44,488 --> 00:10:45,956
Why thank you.

181
00:10:46,289 --> 00:10:49,092
-Not for you. For me. -Huh?

182
00:10:49,292 --> 00:10:51,795
Serving it to you would be a waste.

183
00:10:52,496 --> 00:10:57,234
I pay my taxes. I should consider it a loss to forgo complimentary security.

184
00:10:57,434 --> 00:10:58,301
Now, off you go.

185
00:10:58,502 --> 00:11:00,504
What a cheapskate.

186
00:11:02,239 --> 00:11:04,508
Oh, the party is about to start.

187
00:11:04,808 --> 00:11:07,277
Argh! Chief, I'm sorry.

188
00:11:07,477 --> 00:11:09,413
I need to use the bathroom.

189
00:11:10,213 --> 00:11:12,849
Hey! No more than ten centimeters of toilet paper!

190
00:11:13,083 --> 00:11:15,152
And don't run! You'll dent the carpet!

191
00:11:18,989 --> 00:11:21,058
The girls' dorm is right there.

192
00:11:21,258 --> 00:11:23,827
I can get in and out without the chief noticing.

193
00:11:24,061 --> 00:11:27,164
And also, is this really a bathroom?

194
00:11:27,397 --> 00:11:29,099
"KATSUSHIKA POLICE WOMEN'S DORM"

195
00:11:29,433 --> 00:11:32,602
You invited that Kameari caveman?

196
00:11:33,136 --> 00:11:35,605
This sucks. He's the worst of the worst!

197
00:11:35,806 --> 00:11:37,307
She's right.

198
00:11:37,874 --> 00:11:43,447
Come on, it's Ryo-chan's birthday today. Just put up with him a little.

199
00:11:43,647 --> 00:11:46,883
But he's on duty right now, so he might not be able to come.

200
00:11:47,117 --> 00:11:48,452
You never know with him.

201
00:11:48,652 --> 00:11:50,854
He's like a cockroach. Shows up anywhere.

202
00:11:51,088 --> 00:11:54,658
Yeah. You just turn around, and suddenly he's there.

203
00:11:55,358 --> 00:11:56,560
Sorry to be a roach.

204
00:11:57,027 --> 00:12:01,098
Oh? Looks pretty shabby after just seeing a set that cost 500 million yen.

205
00:12:01,298 --> 00:12:03,900
-500 million? -So? If you don't like it, leave!

206
00:12:04,134 --> 00:12:05,902
-Yeah! -Cool your jets.

207
00:12:06,136 --> 00:12:07,537
Come on, let's party!

208
00:12:09,539 --> 00:12:11,675
Ryo-chan, what about your posting?

209
00:12:12,275 --> 00:12:13,643
Yeah, it's fine.

210
00:12:13,844 --> 00:12:16,646
Huh, this tastes weird. Did you guys cook it properly?

211
00:12:30,594 --> 00:12:33,497
Hmm, not bad. Quite tasty.

212
00:12:44,508 --> 00:12:45,742
This is good.

213
00:12:48,745 --> 00:12:51,781
We'd like to order thirty more portions.

214
00:12:52,015 --> 00:12:52,782
Yes, please.

215
00:12:53,016 --> 00:12:56,052
Okay, no problem. Thank you.

216
00:12:56,253 --> 00:12:58,188
Hey, Reiko! Is the sushi here yet?

217
00:12:58,488 --> 00:13:01,224
It won't be long now. We ordered a lot.

218
00:13:01,491 --> 00:13:03,960
How are you still not full?

219
00:13:04,928 --> 00:13:08,632
I've always got room for sushi. It goes into a separate stomach.

220
00:13:09,232 --> 00:13:13,270
A separate stomach? More like a trash chute.

221
00:13:13,503 --> 00:13:17,440
This is the worst. He'd better be grateful it was Reiko who invited him...

222
00:13:21,211 --> 00:13:26,783
So long as the chief doesn't find out, this March 3 might actually be a good day.

223
00:13:26,983 --> 00:13:27,784
Hmm?

224
00:13:29,786 --> 00:13:31,955
Yes, it's me. Ryotsu.

225
00:13:32,188 --> 00:13:33,456
Huh? Oh, it's not mine.

226
00:13:33,823 --> 00:13:34,958
Yes, this is Ohara.

227
00:13:35,192 --> 00:13:36,826
Oh, it's Chief Ohara.

228
00:13:37,894 --> 00:13:42,132
Yes, yes. Don't worry, Superintendent. We're keeping our eyes peeled as we speak.

229
00:13:42,566 --> 00:13:44,634
No, nothing to report.

230
00:13:44,834 --> 00:13:46,303
Huh? Ryotsu worries you?

231
00:13:46,836 --> 00:13:48,939
No, I'll make sure to tell him.

232
00:13:49,139 --> 00:13:52,542
He's actually pretty useful in times like these.

233
00:13:53,410 --> 00:13:55,312
Y-Yes, this is Ryotsu.

234
00:13:55,545 --> 00:13:57,480
It's me. You still in the bathroom?

235
00:13:57,681 --> 00:14:00,784
Yeah, it just won't seem to come out. Ungh...!

236
00:14:00,984 --> 00:14:03,220
What are you doing, Kankichi Ryotsu?

237
00:14:03,787 --> 00:14:05,755
What was that? Is someone there?

238
00:14:05,956 --> 00:14:07,657
No, it's nothing.

239
00:14:07,857 --> 00:14:10,093
If you're on duty, get back to work.

240
00:14:10,293 --> 00:14:12,128
-Who's there, Ryotsu? -Shut up!

241
00:14:12,329 --> 00:14:14,598
What? Stay there. I'm coming for you.

242
00:14:14,798 --> 00:14:17,400
No, no, there's no need for that...

243
00:14:18,301 --> 00:14:19,869
What are you going to do?

244
00:14:20,103 --> 00:14:22,772
I'll go back. Leave me some sushi.

245
00:14:25,575 --> 00:14:27,978
Honestly. What the heck is he doing?

246
00:14:29,879 --> 00:14:33,149
Oh no, I ate too much.

247
00:14:35,051 --> 00:14:36,319
Good grief.

248
00:14:36,519 --> 00:14:37,320
Hmm?

249
00:14:41,625 --> 00:14:43,693
Hey, Ryotsu! Are you in there?

250
00:14:43,893 --> 00:14:46,830
Ryotsu. Ryotsu! What are you doing?

251
00:14:47,030 --> 00:14:48,365
This is bad...

252
00:14:48,598 --> 00:14:50,033
Ryotsu! Ryotsu!

253
00:14:50,667 --> 00:14:53,036
Hey! Come out at once!

254
00:14:55,872 --> 00:15:00,377
Oh, sorry. I hadn't been for a whole week...

255
00:15:00,677 --> 00:15:03,813
That's a big gut for someone who just let out a week's worth.

256
00:15:04,014 --> 00:15:05,448
Oh, well, that's...

257
00:15:05,649 --> 00:15:08,852
Anyway, I'll go and guard the hina dolls.

258
00:15:09,486 --> 00:15:10,720
-Huh? -Excuse me.

259
00:15:12,389 --> 00:15:15,091
Wow... So this is his bathroom?

260
00:15:23,300 --> 00:15:24,768
Phew...

261
00:15:25,101 --> 00:15:29,072
That was close. He's onto me for sure.

262
00:15:31,107 --> 00:15:31,908
Hmph!

263
00:15:32,208 --> 00:15:34,177
500-million-yen hina dolls.

264
00:15:34,644 --> 00:15:37,914
Who spends that much on dolls?

265
00:15:38,581 --> 00:15:43,420
Paper's all you need, so long as you put your heart into it.

266
00:15:43,653 --> 00:15:48,191
And besides, with a fancy set like this, losing even one doll would be...

267
00:15:49,225 --> 00:15:50,026
Huh?

268
00:15:56,199 --> 00:15:58,668
No... It's gone!

269
00:15:59,202 --> 00:16:04,240
It's gone! One of them is missing!

270
00:16:04,607 --> 00:16:08,278
No, no, no! This is bad!

271
00:16:08,511 --> 00:16:09,446
Uh-oh...

272
00:16:09,679 --> 00:16:13,750
They cost 500 million all together, so to lose one... to lose only one...

273
00:16:13,950 --> 00:16:18,455
Huh, what's that worth? One, two, three...

274
00:16:20,523 --> 00:16:21,958
Tens of millions of yen!

275
00:16:22,459 --> 00:16:24,594
I can't afford that... Damn it!

276
00:16:24,794 --> 00:16:27,464
It happened while I was at the girls' dorm. Ugh...

277
00:16:27,697 --> 00:16:28,298
Wait...

278
00:16:31,701 --> 00:16:33,570
Yes! The one in the girls' dorm!

279
00:16:33,837 --> 00:16:34,637
All right!

280
00:16:38,007 --> 00:16:41,411
-What's wrong, Ryotsu? -T-T-Toilet! Need the toilet!

281
00:16:41,911 --> 00:16:43,646
What, again?

282
00:16:43,980 --> 00:16:44,981
He's so restless.

283
00:16:45,915 --> 00:16:47,417
Wow!

284
00:16:47,617 --> 00:16:49,953
I wonder if Ryo-chan's really coming back?

285
00:16:50,153 --> 00:16:51,955
The sushi just arrived.

286
00:16:52,155 --> 00:16:54,324
-Let's just leave him. -Exactly.

287
00:16:54,991 --> 00:16:56,826
Yum! Scrumdiddlyumptious!

288
00:16:57,026 --> 00:16:59,329
-Mmm! -It looks so good.

289
00:17:02,098 --> 00:17:04,134
-Huh? -What's this?

290
00:17:04,334 --> 00:17:05,335
It's insecticide!

291
00:17:11,608 --> 00:17:12,742
Is everyone okay?

292
00:17:14,811 --> 00:17:15,945
The sushi!

293
00:17:16,346 --> 00:17:19,349
Ugh, this is more important right now.

294
00:17:22,886 --> 00:17:23,853
It stinks!

295
00:17:27,157 --> 00:17:28,358
-Ah! -Huh?

296
00:17:32,328 --> 00:17:34,063
Uh-oh, the head...

297
00:17:34,297 --> 00:17:36,666
-Who's there? Ryo-chan? -Eep!

298
00:17:43,339 --> 00:17:45,375
I'm good so long as no one touches it.

299
00:17:45,608 --> 00:17:48,445
And that cheapskate won't let anyone touch it.

300
00:17:48,778 --> 00:17:49,879
-Ryotsu. -Yikes!

301
00:17:50,680 --> 00:17:52,982
-What are you doing? -Nothing at all!

302
00:17:53,183 --> 00:17:55,452
I'm worried about you guarding them.

303
00:17:55,652 --> 00:17:57,921
-I'll take your place. -Oh, but...

304
00:17:58,221 --> 00:18:00,557
Knowing you, with 500 million yen at stake,

305
00:18:00,790 --> 00:18:03,827
you might secretly swap the dolls for fakes.

306
00:18:04,160 --> 00:18:06,463
D-Don't be ridiculous!

307
00:18:06,930 --> 00:18:10,999
Besides, I'll bet your face scares the poor dolls.

308
00:18:11,201 --> 00:18:13,470
-That's nonsense. -Just go!

309
00:18:13,670 --> 00:18:16,005
Y-Yes, sir.

310
00:18:21,077 --> 00:18:22,512
He won't notice, will he?

311
00:18:24,848 --> 00:18:25,648
Hmm...

312
00:18:26,216 --> 00:18:29,752
Up close, they're definitely top-notch. What superior craftsmanship.

313
00:18:29,953 --> 00:18:32,222
Ugh... Please don't let him notice.

314
00:18:32,589 --> 00:18:34,591
Truly a feast for the eyes.

315
00:18:34,824 --> 00:18:36,926
And this empress doll is gorgeous.

316
00:18:37,126 --> 00:18:40,096
No, please don't stare...

317
00:18:40,597 --> 00:18:41,397
Hmm?

318
00:18:43,233 --> 00:18:44,567
What's this?

319
00:18:59,449 --> 00:19:00,450
Oh my gosh!

320
00:19:00,683 --> 00:19:02,418
He noticed! Huh?

321
00:19:02,919 --> 00:19:05,622
I... What have I done?

322
00:19:06,122 --> 00:19:07,757
He thinks he broke it.

323
00:19:07,957 --> 00:19:10,093
Hmm, this gives me an idea...

324
00:19:12,795 --> 00:19:13,863
Chief!

325
00:19:14,864 --> 00:19:16,999
What are you doing there?

326
00:19:17,233 --> 00:19:17,934
Oh?

327
00:19:18,401 --> 00:19:21,404
Oh no! Did you just...

328
00:19:22,739 --> 00:19:26,342
Chief! What a terrible person you are.

329
00:19:26,576 --> 00:19:30,246
I just grazed it a little. I'm sorry.

330
00:19:30,446 --> 00:19:33,016
They cost 500 million yen.

331
00:19:33,750 --> 00:19:35,618
The empress must be 50 million.

332
00:19:35,818 --> 00:19:38,588
No... As the leading lady of the dolls...

333
00:19:39,088 --> 00:19:41,090
she's gotta be at least 100 million!

334
00:19:43,793 --> 00:19:45,495
Whatever's going on in here?

335
00:19:47,997 --> 00:19:50,333
The... The empress doll...

336
00:19:50,567 --> 00:19:51,334
-Mama! -Mama!

337
00:19:51,568 --> 00:19:52,835
Chief, how could you?

338
00:19:54,137 --> 00:19:56,439
I'm so sorry, Kingaichi-san.

339
00:19:57,373 --> 00:20:01,511
I will make it up to you, even if it takes the rest of my life.

340
00:20:02,045 --> 00:20:06,316
Even if you work 24 hours a day for the rest of your life, it won't be enough.

341
00:20:06,816 --> 00:20:09,819
His wife will have to work too. And his daughter.

342
00:20:10,019 --> 00:20:16,292
Oh, how tragic! The Ohara family is ruined because of the chief's mistake!

343
00:20:16,492 --> 00:20:17,327
I understand.

344
00:20:18,027 --> 00:20:20,663
I was tasked with protecting a citizen's property.

345
00:20:20,863 --> 00:20:24,834
To be such a reckless police officer... Why, it is unforgiveable.

346
00:20:25,468 --> 00:20:27,236
I will take full responsibility.

347
00:20:27,470 --> 00:20:32,375
I hereby resign from the police force, and I will use my payout as compensation.

348
00:20:32,608 --> 00:20:33,676
Wait, no...

349
00:20:33,876 --> 00:20:37,380
Um, Chief, you don't have to go that far.

350
00:20:37,614 --> 00:20:38,982
Do not stop me, Ryotsu.

351
00:20:39,182 --> 00:20:41,684
Your payout wouldn't come close to covering it!

352
00:20:41,884 --> 00:20:43,519
Huh? Hold on, that's...

353
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:47,056
I promise I will pay you back, even if I have to sell my house.

354
00:20:47,256 --> 00:20:48,825
Oh no!

355
00:20:49,392 --> 00:20:51,894
Are you going to lose your house, Mister?

356
00:20:53,496 --> 00:20:57,367
It can't be helped, little lady. This is my fault.

357
00:20:57,567 --> 00:21:02,271
When you make a mistake, you must apologize and make amends.

358
00:21:02,505 --> 00:21:07,643
To avoid your responsibilities is the worst thing you can do.

359
00:21:11,180 --> 00:21:13,916
Ch-Chief! Actually, um, I...

360
00:21:14,450 --> 00:21:18,087
Ryotsu, let's not cause them any more trouble.

361
00:21:18,287 --> 00:21:22,025
I'll go submit my resignation letter to headquarters right away.

362
00:21:22,659 --> 00:21:23,259
Huh?

363
00:21:26,396 --> 00:21:28,865
I'm sorry!

364
00:21:29,732 --> 00:21:31,434
What's going on?

365
00:21:31,668 --> 00:21:34,370
We were playing in this room...

366
00:21:36,439 --> 00:21:37,907
-Over here! -Wait!

367
00:21:44,547 --> 00:21:47,116
We broke the hina doll.

368
00:21:49,552 --> 00:21:51,320
We thought we'd get in trouble,

369
00:21:51,554 --> 00:21:55,792
so we wrote that threat and tried to make it look like a thief stole it.

370
00:21:56,092 --> 00:21:57,794
What?

371
00:21:58,327 --> 00:21:59,429
I'm sorry!

372
00:21:59,629 --> 00:22:02,799
We broke your beloved hina doll!

373
00:22:03,032 --> 00:22:03,800
I'm sorry!

374
00:22:04,233 --> 00:22:06,936
I... I...

375
00:22:21,984 --> 00:22:23,953
I'm glad you're not hurt.

376
00:22:25,988 --> 00:22:27,990
Whose hina doll is this, anyway?

377
00:22:28,191 --> 00:22:31,728
-I had it made for you, Amari. Right? -Papa...

378
00:22:32,061 --> 00:22:33,463
Never you fret.

379
00:22:33,663 --> 00:22:38,668
Papa doesn't care for those hina dolls. Papa only cares about you two.

380
00:22:39,268 --> 00:22:40,203
Papa...

381
00:22:40,436 --> 00:22:41,671
Papa, I'm so sorry!

382
00:22:41,904 --> 00:22:43,206
I'm sorry!

383
00:22:43,439 --> 00:22:45,508
There, there.

384
00:22:45,741 --> 00:22:48,077
But you shouldn't have kept this from me.

385
00:22:48,277 --> 00:22:52,682
As the nice police officer said, all you have to do is apologize, right?

386
00:22:52,949 --> 00:22:53,950
Yeah...

387
00:22:54,617 --> 00:22:58,988
Well, that's a happy ending, isn't it, Chief?

388
00:22:59,188 --> 00:23:00,523
Yes...

389
00:23:00,757 --> 00:23:03,493
But then where did this hina doll come from?

390
00:23:03,693 --> 00:23:04,494
Gulp!

391
00:23:04,927 --> 00:23:07,697
Could this be... your doing?

392
00:23:07,930 --> 00:23:09,932
N-No, not exactly. I just...

393
00:23:10,133 --> 00:23:12,668
Well, I borrowed it from the girls' dorm.

394
00:23:12,869 --> 00:23:16,472
So you knew that the one I broke was a fake?

395
00:23:16,672 --> 00:23:18,641
No, well, I just...

396
00:23:27,350 --> 00:23:28,151
Mama!

397
00:23:30,186 --> 00:23:32,355
I'm sorry. I did it.

398
00:23:33,122 --> 00:23:35,324
This is my earnest apology, so...

399
00:23:35,525 --> 00:23:37,426
That only applies to my children!

400
00:23:38,194 --> 00:23:41,497
I'll have you toil the rest of your life to pay me back.

401
00:23:43,266 --> 00:23:47,904
Please work him as hard as you like. You hear that, Ryotsu?

402
00:23:48,137 --> 00:23:50,506
What? No, Chief!

403
00:23:51,140 --> 00:23:54,610
I knew it! Nothing good ever comes on March 3!

404
00:23:54,844 --> 00:23:55,978
Damn it all!

405
00:23:56,512 --> 00:24:00,583
I hate Girls' Day!
